<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγκῠρ-έω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εκύρησα</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έκυρσα</span> (v. infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>come together by chance</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή πως συγκύρσειαν ὁδῷ ἔνι μώνυχες
					ἵπποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.435
				</span></i>
			; of ships, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.92
			</span></i>; <i>meet with</i> an accident, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇδε συγκῦρσαι τύχῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1404
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήτεσι πολλοῖς συγκεκυρηκέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					17.106
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραγικοῖς πάθεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					20.21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτυχίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mort.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἓν μοίρας συνέκυρσας</span>
			<i>art involved</i> in one and the same fate, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1172
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.
				part., 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυγχάνω, συνέκυρσε θέων</span>
			
			<i>happened</i> to be running, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				53
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ συνεκύρησε . . παραπεσοῦσα
				νηῦς</span> whether it fell in the way <i>by chance</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.87
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of events
			and accidents, <i>happen, occur</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢν δέ τι δεινὸν συγκύρσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					698
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδε οἶδα . . τοῖσι ἐν Ἰταλίῃ
					συγκυρήσαντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. μοι ἡδονά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1448
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς τύχα μοι
			συγκυρήσει</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IT</u>
				874
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ συγκυρήσαντα</span>
			<i>what had occurred</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.119
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃ καὶ συνεκύρησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.65.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.132
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ παρὰ τοῦ δαιμονίου -ήσαντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					5.56
				</span></i>
			: impers., c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνεκύρησε γενέσθαι</span>
			<i>it came to pass</i> that . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.90
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Oct.</u>
				10
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἔχθος τὸ ἐς Λακεδαιμονίους
					συγκεκυρημένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.37
				</span></i>
			 (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγκεκρημένον</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of places, <i>to be
				contiguous to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώραις -οῦσαν θάλατταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.59.7
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arist.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐσεβὼν καὶ ταῖς -ούσαις αὐτῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Nu.</u>
					21.25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγκύρω</span>
			.</div>
